                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Alright, so it's a little tough and confusing at first...and probably after.  Controls...are a little awkward.  It seems like it wants me to use A, S, D, Z, and X, as well as the arrow keys AND the mouse...  Since I don't have three hands, that can sometimes throw me off a little, but there is an option in dungeons to auto-move so you aren't using the arrows.  When in dungeons, battle is fairly simple (and this is an evaluation Before learning any skills...).  You need to remember to use the X key to block attacks.  There is a little skill involved in dodging, striking, and blocking so you don't die.  However, this game has a system of Morality.  You can do bad deeds, and failing to do good deeds (or failing an adventure) takes from your Morality.  I like how I can lose in a dungeon, and still not have a game over.\nWhat I learned after gaining 4 levels is that the game assumes you're Not an idiot.  You have to manually go to the status screen on the map and allocate skill points to your character.  You can customize her a little to your play style.  I bought this on impulse and don't know how long the game is, or what else it has to offer, but I like how you can go into towns and talk with people to take on contracts (jobs) for money.  You can also ask various people to fight with you (but it seems you can only have 1 partner at a time.)  Some fight up close, and others do from a distance.  Again, you have a choice to match your specific play style.\nThe game has great art and fun cut scenes when you \"die\" in a dungeon.  It's not the easiest game to play, but I look forward to seeing what else this thing has to offer.  This is already a fun little romp, though probably not for everyone.",
